CM_ BO_ 228 "Speed and heading data coming off of MyLaps racelink unit. Currently at 200 ms but WIP to bump up the update rate. This is for future improvement of purple flag behaviour by providing a redundant source of speed. ";
CM_ BO_ 226 "GPS data from MyLaps racelink unit. Currently at 200 ms but WIP to bump up the update rate.  ";
CM_ BO_ 1406 "AV24 vehicle will have virtual dash switches to perform low-level software functions like:

a) Traction Control
b) Pit Speed Limiter 
c) Push2Pass
d) Dynamic gain control for steering and brakes

The switch field has description of the type of switch (two-position, multi-pos etc.) and the corresponding function mapped to it in individual comments

CT are expected to respond to the switches in some form.

";
CM_ SG_ 1406 driver_traction_aim_switch "Switch Position: 0 (TC is OFF)
Switch Position: 1 (TC is ON and least aggressive - will allow the most wheel slip)
Swicth Position: 2 (TC is ON and less aggressive - will allow more wheel slip)
Switch Position: 3 (TC is ON and aggressive - will allow less wheel slip)
Switch Position: 4 (TC is ON and most aggressive - will allow the least wheel slip)";
CM_ SG_ 1406 driver_traction_range_switch "Switch Position: 0 (TC is ON and torque cut is moderate/default - Note: Traction Aim switch needs to be non-zero)
Switch Position: 1 (TC is ON and torque cut is most gradual i.e. it will allow most additional wheel slip on top of the aim)
Swicth Position: 2 (TC is ON and torque cut is less gradual than 1)
Switch Position: 3 (TC is ON and torque cut is aggressive)
Switch Position: 4 (TC is ON and torque cut is most aggressive. Most favorable in cold and damp conditions)";
CM_ SG_ 1406 brake_bias_aim_switch "Switch Position: 0 (Bias aimed is 50%)
Switch Position: 1 (Bias aimed is 51%)
Swicth Position: 2 (Bias aimed is 52%)
Switch Position: 3 (Bias aimed is 53%)
Switch Position: 4 (Bias aimed is 54%)
Switch Position: 5 (Bias aimed is 55%)
Swicth Position: 6 (Bias aimed is 56%)
Switch Position: 7 (Bias aimed is 57%)
Switch Position: 8 (Bias aimed is 58%)
Switch Position: 9 (Gives independant front and rear wheels brake control)";
CM_ SG_ 1406 drive_steering_gain_cntrl_switch "Switch Position: 0 (default raptor gains used - last saved values through calibration tool)
Switch Position: 1 (PID gains expected from the team if switched to 1) 

Safety: 

1) Nothing is transmitted on this signal - If nothing is ever transmitted - Raptor will read this as \"zero\" meaning default gains will be used.

2) Team transmits \"one\" but no gains are transmitted - Raptor will detect this and stick with default gains. The gains should always be transmitted if the switch is changed to \"one\". If not done correctly, can cause major system malfunction

3) Team switches back to \"zero\" but gains are still being published - This is fine and indeed prefered. It is suggested that the teams always transmit the gains (even if the dynamic gain control is not being used).  

Prefered mode of operation:
PID values and the switch can be parametrized and kept changeable thru base station.
Safety logic ensuring that the PID values are saturated to realistic values before sent to raptor.  ";
CM_ SG_ 1406 push2pass_switch "Switch Position: 0 (Driver does not command P2P)
Switch Position: 1 (Driver commands P2P)";
CM_ SG_ 1406 drive_steering_FF_cntrl_switch "Switch Position: 0 (Driver does not want/wants to operate with default raptor FF settings)
Switch Position: 1 (Driver wants to send FF gain online)";
CM_ BO_ 1450 "Long,Lat and Vertical G forces (Tx to Raptor at 100Hz) 
Source: Novatel Top/Bottom. Needed for Traction Control at MoTeC.  ";
